                <pb facs="0218" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/60: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-05-24T19:00:00-04:00">May 24, 1933—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Your 67, May 12, 4 p.m. This Government is taking a strong stand against the
                    whole system of exchange controls and is urging other governments to take
                    appropriate steps in order to remove this obstacle to trade. As long as there is
                    any hope of practical achievement at London in this direction we do not wish to
                    enter into any commercial arrangement recognizing exchange control.</p>
                <p>If it turns out that no progress can be made at London in this regard we shall
                    doubtless be prepared to consider a treaty with Chile along the lines you
                    suggest.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
